From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tai Nguyen <tai.nguyen@mobilio.asia>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:38:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] 2026-11-11 16:38 - Mac: frame-rate counter badge in the game
 window (DM_SHOW_FPS)

- front_mac.m draws a small badge at the top left of the game's window when DM_SHOW_FPS=1, as the iPhone's: the frames put on screen in the last second (mtl_present_count)
- settings.tsv offers Frame-rate counter on the Mac too, off by default there. The iPhone keeps the build's default
- test_launcher_settings and docs/settings.md follow

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: A Mac game had no small frame-rate readout: only Apple's full Metal performance HUD. The iPhone app already has the badge
Issue: none (a personal fork feature, not proposed to LNPANDY/NX2Apple)

